# beatmania IIDX 2nd style (Twinkle): the scripted game of bmiidx2-play.his with the key at sound
# select 62 frames later (3662), on the cabinet's 4x CD drive. That timing puts the end of one of the
# song's hard disk reads between two instructions of the sound board's 60 Hz interrupt handler: the
# disk's handler then writes the control register with both interrupts' enables down. Each must be
# acknowledged (runtime/twinkle/spuctrl.h); with MAME's rule (HK_TW_ONE_ACK=1) the sound board never
# leaves the disk's handler and the game stops with E730:HDD READ ERROR instead of playing the stage
# (GitHub issue 19). A regress case, not an oracle script: MAME's driver has that rule.
game bmiidx2

at 1800 press "Coin 1" 8
at 1830 press "Coin 1" 8
at 2700 press "1 Player Start" 8
at 3000 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
at 3662 press "P1-1 (SW1)" 8
